# ============================================================================
# GPLOT Model Info Table (Python format)
#
# Column 1: Model ID (ATCF TECH code)
# Column 2: Display label (shown in plot legends)
# Column 3: matplotlib marker string
#           ('o','s','^','v','<','>','*','D','d','p','h','8','P','X','+','x','.')
# Column 4: matplotlib color value. May be any of:
#             - A CSS4/X11 named color (e.g. 'blue', 'darkgoldenrod')
#             - An xkcd color with the 'xkcd:' prefix (e.g. 'xkcd:deep pink')
#             - A hex value (e.g. '#8B0A50')
#             - A grayscale float string in [0,1] (e.g. '0.25')
# Column 5: Long name (optional)
#
# Fields are separated by commas.  Lines starting with '#' are comments.
# This file supersedes ModelInfo.dat (which uses NCL marker indices and
# NCL-only X11 color names).  Python modules prefer this file when present.
# ============================================================================

